# Configuration

The connector is configured through OSGi, not environment variables. The
shipped config is:

```
/apps/example/translategemma/config/com.example.aem.translation.impl.TranslateGemmaTranslationServiceImpl.xml
```

## Properties

| PID attribute | Type | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `projectId` | String | *(empty)* | GCP project. Empty = ambient ADC project. |
| `location` | String | `us-central1` | Vertex AI region. |
| `enabled` | Boolean | `true` | If false, `isServiceAvailable()` returns false and translation projects skip this connector. |
| `modelName` | String | `gemma-3-27b-it` | Model identifier passed to Vertex AI. |
| `defaultContentCategory` | String | `general` | Content category reported to AEM. |
| `enableFallbackProviders` | Boolean | `true` | Call other `TranslationProvider`s when Gemma fails. |
| `enableSentimentAnalysis` | Boolean | `false` | Attach a sentiment/quality heuristic to prompts. |
| `enableComplianceCheck` | Boolean | `false` | Attach a compliance heuristic to prompts. |
| `retryMaxAttempts` | Long | 3 | |
| `retryWaitDurationMs` | Long | 1000 | |
| `circuitBreakerFailureRateThreshold` | Long | 50 | Percent. |
| `circuitBreakerSlowCallRateThreshold` | Long | 100 | Percent. |
| `circuitBreakerSlowCallDurationMs` | Long | 5000 | |
| `circuitBreakerWaitDurationS` | Long | 30 | |
| `enableCaching` | Boolean | `true` | Caffeine cache in memory. |
| `cacheMaxSize` | Long | 1000 | |
| `cacheExpireAfterMinutes` | Long | 60 | |
| `enableMetrics` | Boolean | `true` | Local meter registry (not exported to any backend). |

## Credentials

The Vertex AI SDK uses Application Default Credentials. Point the AEM JVM at a
service account:

```bash
export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/path/to/service-account.json
```

or rely on the machine identity (GKE Workload Identity, GCE metadata, etc.).

## Environment variables on AEM as a Cloud Service

Cloud Manager environment variables are only read by OSGi configs that reference
them with `${env:NAME}` placeholders. If you want that, add a config containing:

```xml
<jcr:root jcr:primaryType="sling:OsgiConfig" projectId="${env:GCP_PROJECT_ID}" location="${env:GCP_LOCATION}"/>
```

Do not put service-account JSON in Cloud Manager variables; mount/attach
credentials through the normal GCP mechanism instead.
